+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates tool inputs against each registered tool's declared JSON Schema (`inputSchema`) before invoking the executor. Invalid inputs return a `ToolResponse` describing the failing property paths and constraints so the model can self-correct within the orchestrator's tool-round loop, while `Unknown tool: <name>` remains the only case where `execute` throws.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and constraint without invoking the executor, and never echoes offending input values in the returned text or log lines ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the failing property and constraint without calling the executor or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only: valid input passes through unmodified without coercing types, applying schema defaults, or stripping unlisted extra properties ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unmodified without coercing types or applying defaults](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L70)).
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when its inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L109)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition per call and validates against the schema returned for that call rather than a stale cached schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L124)).
+- When `createChatOrchestrator` receives a malformed tool call, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns the rejection as a `tool_result` message so the model can retry within the tool-round budget and `processMessage` resolves ([validated by: resolves when a rejected tool call is retried with valid input and exposes the rejection to the provider](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L22)).
+- Static tool schemas are compiled once at registration time and reused across subsequent `execute` calls rather than recompiled on each call.
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` when asked to execute an unregistered tool name.
